# The panel .kicad_pcb is a ~9.7 MB intermediate: scripts/panelize.py rebuilds it from
# PCB/solar-glow-drh-v4_0.kicad_pcb on every PCB push, so committing it would add a
# fresh blob that size to an already 200 MB+ repo each time, for a file nobody reads.
# The FAB SET generated from it (gerbers, drills, zip) IS committed under Generated/panel
# and is what gets uploaded to PCBWay.
#
# Need the panel board itself? Rebuild it:  python3 scripts/panelize.py
Generated/panel/*.kicad_pcb

# ...and its RULEBOOK, copied beside it by panelize.py since 2026-08-10. KiCad resolves both
# by basename next to the .kicad_pcb, and zone fills read from both -- netclass clearances from
# the .kicad_pro, the custom floors from the .kicad_dru. They exist so KiBot's check_zone_fills
# refills the panel against the CARD's rules; without them it silently falls back to KiCad
# defaults, which are looser, so every solid pour comes out smaller (GND_B_AVR_ISLAND: 20.91 mm2
# vs 30.27). Derived copies of files already committed under PCB/ -- ignore them for the same
# reason as the panel board itself.
Generated/panel/*.kicad_pro
Generated/panel/*.kicad_dru

# kicad-cli drops a .kicad_prl (per-user VIEW STATE -- active layer, opacities) beside any
# board it opens, including the uncommitted panel board above. The commit-back's
# `git add -A Generated` swept one in once; it is not a fab artifact, and without this line
# deleting it just resurrects on the next run (the bc50e41 lesson, in miniature).
Generated/**/*.kicad_prl

# KiCad's project lock file. Harmless, but it now appears in a plain checkout because CI
# runs kicad-cli against PCB/ in-repo (scripts/render.py), and kicad-cli takes the lock the
# same way the GUI does. Never worth committing.
~*.lck

# enclosure/part_heights.py is imported by the generators and by check_consistency [7],
# so a plain run leaves a __pycache__ beside it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
